# Slice 282 probe: a rebound callable field read as a value: `@: g Box\f` holds what stands there, and a later write of the field does not move g.  Entry 7.
Box:
    fn: f () int
        return: 1
    end: f
end: Box
fn: two () int
    return: 2
end: two
fn: three () int
    return: 3
end: three
fn: run () int
    @: Box\f two
    @: g Box\f
    @: Box\f three
    return: g() * 10 + Box\f()
end: run
int: code 7
if: run() != 23
    code: 12
---
sendMessage: exit(exit_code: code; stdout: ""; stderr: "")
